{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1761135,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"purple_un","paid":0,"title":"National Young Programmers Olympiad","festival_id":null,"organization_id":1731609,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-09-24T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-10T18:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"hackathons","public_url":"hackathons\/national-young-programmers-olympiad-polaris-school-of-technology-1761135","region":"online","details":"<p><strong>Overview:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>NYPO 2026 &ndash; National Young Programmers Olympiad is a national-level technology competition for students from Classes 8 to 12 across India, organised by Polaris School of Technology and Navneet Education. It is designed to test students on logic, problem-solving, creativity and their ability to build with technology and AI. No prior coding knowledge is required to participate.<\/p>\n<p><strong>The Olympiad has two tracks:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Junior Track: Classes 8&ndash;10<\/li>\n<li>Senior Track: Classes 11&ndash;12<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Students progress through three stages:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Coding Aptitude<\/strong> &ndash; Logical thinking and problem-solving<\/li>\n<li><strong>Video Round<\/strong> &ndash; Demonstrate and communicate their approach to an idea<\/li>\n<li><strong>Vibecoding<\/strong> &ndash; Use code and AI tools to turn ideas into something real<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Registered students will receive preparation material, and the difficulty level is designed separately for each track.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Participants can compete for opportunities and rewards including:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Amazon HQ Bengaluru Visit + Industry Exposure &amp; Mentorship<\/li>\n<li>\u20b910 Lakh Cash Prize<\/li>\n<li>\u20b91 Crore Polaris Scholarship Grant<\/li>\n<li>MacBook Air<\/li>\n<li>$100K worth of Tech Credits<\/li>\n<li>National-level Certificates &amp; Recognition<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Other Details<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><stron